                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support><p>A small fragment of off-white marble, broken on all sides. Rear face is unworked and uneven.</p>
                                    <material ana="#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Docimian #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Pentelic" type="stone.marble" subtype="Docimian|Pentelic" resp="#Coccato" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html">Very fine-grained, homogeneous, white, calcitic marble, likely Docimian, Pentelic. Digital microscopy: heteroblastic to homeoblastic fabric. lunense does not make sense. Sr too low for Goktepe. no smell so unlikely Hymettan (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy, XRD)<note> Petrographic imagery at <ref target="https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic004340">https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic004340</ref></note></material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.plaque" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259">plaque</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">8.8</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">10.1</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm">2.9-3.1</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition ana="#condition.fragment"/>
		    </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout><p>Traces of five lines of Greek letters, with some vacats before initial letters on the left side.</p>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.chiselled" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">chiselled</rs>
                                	<damage ana="#text_condition.incomplete"/>
			</layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote><p>Widely spaced, neatly cut, regular letters of broad module. Alpha has straight bar; eta is wide; Mu has vertical outer strokes and half-length inner strokes; omicron is small and above the line (6mm); phi has a slightly extended vertical (14mm); omega is full size, circular, and open with horizontal feet.</p>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line4">Line 1-4</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm" atLeast="9" atMost="10">9-10</height>
                                </dimensions>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line2">Interlineation line 1 to 2</locus>
                                <dimensions type="interlinear">
                                    <height unit="mm"/>
                                </dimensions>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
